From 4e207cd644d9ebf74032a8c8a831254b13060e10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicola Ferralis <ferralis@generalflash.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:23:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ext: hollow parts, pads first then a large closed cavity
 (family and suite "hollow")

A pump casing is built outside in: the body, flanges and bosses, then a cavity that removes a large
share of the material, so until it is cut the part is far heavier than its target (the S 80
casing core: about 1.5 times after its flange pads). Synthetic cavities remove about 12 % of the
body on average, and v3 read "far over the target volume right after a pad" as a wrong pad and
undid it. New family and suite "hollow": a box or cylinder base, one to three pad groups (flange
pads on an origin plane with an offset that stick out of one side only, alone, patterned along Z
or mirrored, and top bosses), then one or two large closed cavities on XY datum planes (25-75 %
of the body; rectangles, outlines, round in cylinders), optionally a bore from the top. Goals stay
at least 1.25 times over their target after the pads. No new goal keys; earlier suites keep their
goals.
